    content: "# Best Time to Visit Kashmir\n\nKashmir transforms dramatically across the seasons, each offering a distinct palette of experiences. Here's our complete month-by-month guide.\n\n## Spring (March–May)\nMarch brings the first thaw and the famous **Tulip Festival** in Srinagar's Indira Gandhi Memorial Tulip Garden - Asia's largest tulip garden. April-May is ideal for Mughal Gardens and Dal Lake shikara rides.\n\n## Summer (June–August)\nPeak tourist season. Gulmarg's meadows bloom, Sonmarg's meadows turn gold, and Pahalgam offers riverside bliss. Temperatures hover at 20-30°C - perfect escape from India's plains heat.\n\n## Autumn (September–November)\nPerhaps Kashmir's most romantic season - the chinar trees turn crimson and gold, Mughal gardens blaze with colour, and the crowds thin. September is harvest time for saffron in Pampore.\n\n## Winter (December–February)\nFor snow lovers and skiers - Gulmarg's legendary powder skiing is at its peak, Dal Lake may freeze, and the entire valley turns into a snow-globe. Houseboat stays are magical with kangri (fire pots).\n\n**Our recommendation:** April-May for tulips & gardens, September for autumn romance, January for skiing.",
